  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'old-stock-morenci-2-turquoise-cabochon-gemstone-with-pyrite-38-4x23-0-mm-oval-57', '1675001231', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/1675001231/morenci-2-turquoise-cabochon-384-x-230?click_key=5ea596ef-62a5-4ff0-9bb4-7ad5202a8c34%3ALT61b628cc34b738dadd8e91640b36bab97c2c5138&click_sum=18a3e75c&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=turquoise+jewelry&ref=search_grid-969538-15-16&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&sts=1&content_source=5ea596ef-62a5-4ff0-9bb4-7ad5202a8c34%253ALT61b628cc34b738dadd8e91640b36bab97c2c5138',
   'Old Stock Morenci 2 Turquoise Cabochon: Gemstone with Pyrite (38.4x23.0 mm Oval, 57.4 carats)', 'This Morenci 2 Turquoise cabochon is a large oval gemstone measuring 38.4 x 23.0 mm, weighing 57.4 carats. The cabochon has an approximate 6.9 mm dome (total height) and a 2.4 mm girdle (side height), making it ideal for a professional bezel setting. The turquoise has been professionally stabilized like most turquoise from the area. Morenci 2 Turquoise is a highly collectible variety of turquoise sourced from the historic Nacozari mining district in Sonora, Mexico. This classic locality is celebrated for producing turquoise that closely mirror the appearance of traditional Arizona Morenci Turquoise. This heavy, collector-grade cabochon features a unique, mineral-dense palette dominated by extensive, highly polished splashes of metallic iron pyrite matrix that frame pools of deep blue-green and teal turquoise. Due to the high iron content, the stone carries a substantial physical weight and metallic reflectivity, with the polished pyrite acting like small mirrors across the face. The stone consists of solid, stabilized turquoise and matrix with no backing material, remaining structurally sound. It has a flat back and a straight girdle designed specifically for custom metalsmithing. Due to the natural crystalline growth of iron pyrite alongside turquoise, tiny natural vugs or micro pockets are normal for this heavy mineral style, and the face has been well polished to a bright luster. Turquoise is a December birthstone, 11th anniversary gemstone and the State Gemstone of Arizona. Metaphysically, turquoise is considered one of the most powerful healing stones. Throughout history different cultures, including Native Americans, Tibetans and Egyptians, revered its healing powers. Turquoise is said to be a stone of communication and also helps the mental state overall by increasing serenity, creativity, empathy, positive thinking, intuition, happiness and wisdom. It is considered a stone of friendship. Its blue color has come to symbolize the spirit or sky. We have photogr', 'turquoise-jewelry',
