  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'kingman-turquoise-cabochon-oval-arizona-gemstone-29-5-x-21-6-mm-31-6-carats', '1413778142', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/1413778142/kingman-turquoise-cabochon-295-x-216-mm?click_key=2ed48753-436f-4083-9571-6ba7e17e2d61%3ALT2dcfa0a1ca93292f3492936dba255aec19fdd99a&click_sum=843355c3&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=turquoise+jewelry&ref=search_grid-882401-14-19&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&sts=1&content_source=2ed48753-436f-4083-9571-6ba7e17e2d61%253ALT2dcfa0a1ca93292f3492936dba255aec19fdd99a',
   'Kingman Turquoise Cabochon: Oval Arizona Gemstone ( 29.5 x 21.6 mm, 31.6 carats)', 'This Kingman Turquoise cabochon is a 29.5 x 21.6 mm, 31.6 carats, oval gemstone. It has an approximately 6.6 mm dome (total height) and 2.3 mm girdle. The raw stone was mined from the Kingman copper mine in Kingman, Arizona. This is old stock turquoise from the 1980s or 1990s. The turquoise has been stabilized like most turquoise from the area and may have been color enhanced. The cabochon is sky blue with grey splotches, some which include very tiny pyrite sparkles. There is a healed fracture line in this cabochon and we have priced accordingly. Turquoise is a December birthstone, 11th anniversary gemstone and the State Gemstone of Arizona. Metaphysically, turquoise is considered one of the most powerful healing stones. Throughout history different cultures, including Native Americans, Tibetans and Egyptians, revered its healing powers. Turquoise is said to be a stone of communication and also helps the mental state overall by increasing serenity, creativity, empathy, positive thinking, intuition, happiness and wisdom. It is considered a stone of friendship. Its blue color has come to symbolize the spirit or sky. The photos were taken outside in the Arizona sun. Although we strive for color accuracy, computer monitors and cellphone screens may differ. Blues are difficult to capture precisely and reds may appear brighter. Colors may appear less bright under indoor lighting. We take great pride in our cabochons, making each cabochon in a process that takes up to 2-3 hours. Our cabochons have rounded domed tops, straight sides (girdle) and a flat bottom. Typically, tops are polished with 8 steps and bottoms 7 steps. We cut our stones for the best patterns and colors. Due to our handmade process, there may be some variation in size. All cabochons are natural and may have minor imperfections. 100% American and American-made! Find more cabochons in our "Cabochons" category at www.prospectingarizona.etsy.com. Follow us on Facebook and Instagram for updates and more inform', 'accessories',
